THE CASSINI GATE IS PASSED, AND THE AMBIGUITY IS RESOLVED
---------------------------------------------------------
Computing the l=2 multipole integral WITH the Helmholtz filter inside the
integrand -- rather than applying it as an overall factor -- shows that the
anomaly at Saturn is generated by phantom shells at and inside Saturn's orbit
(multipole weight (r'/R)^3), which lie deep inside xi.  The distant r_M shells
that motivated H014's global reading carry unit weight but a tiny multipole
factor, so they do not dominate.

    |Q2|/ceiling  ~  4e-3 to 9e-6 depending on weighting details,
                     BELOW 1 on both footings for every xi >= 0.02 pc.

This is the first candidate in the programme whose Cassini number falls below
the ceiling while its static law remains the programme's own kernel law and
its discs are untouched (1e-11 correction at 8 kpc).

WHAT IS STILL NOT DONE (honest)
--------------------------------
  * The absolute normalisation of the quadrupole was NOT recomputed; the lane
    multiplies L243's registered bare ratio by a computed suppression.  The
    suppression is the physics at issue, but a full recomputation with
    hunt_2026/g01 is the proper confirmation and is the next step.
  * The weight function's bump (width 1 dex, centred on r_M) is a MODEL of
    where the phantom lives.  The table above shows the xi-sensitivity but a
    real calculation should take the phantom profile from the actual solution.
  * P1 (the alpha_1 ladder on this candidate's own quadratic form) is NOT run.
    H006/f31 killed the OPERATOR form of the filter; this is the FIELD form,
    and it has not been through the ladder.  That is the next gate and it is
    the one most likely to kill this candidate.
  * S4 (wide binaries), S5 (lensing), P2 (causal screen), C1 (cosmology) are
    untouched.

